  "published": "2026-07-25T20:59:31.657Z",
  "releaseNotes": "TCMProject.Web: error responses no longer leak stack traces in Production. ExceptionMiddleware now keeps the full detail (stack trace, Source, TargetSite) in the log — which is what feeds the observability stack — while the HTTP body carries only the exception message chain when the environment is Production; outside Production the response is unchanged. Downstream error bodies replayed by the gateway (ResponseException) are sanitised the same way. PermissionAuthorizationHandler asks IsAuthenticated() before GetUserLogged(), so an unauthenticated request to an endpoint with [HasPermission] returns 401 instead of the 500 it threw before, and the handler no longer writes the caller's permission blob to stdout on every request. Behavioural change to error payloads in Production only; no API surface removed.",
